"\\:py\\:data\\:\\`...\\<Ellipsis\\>\\`\\]`"
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.edge_corner_keys:1 of
msgid "Return the keys of the two corners at the ends of an edge."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.edge_neighbour_edge_keys:1 of
msgid "Return the keys of the (up to four) edges that touch an edge at a corner."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.edge_pixel_offset:1 of
msgid "Return the pixel offset of an edge center, relative to the hex center."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.edge_pixel_offsets:1 of
msgid "Return the pixel offsets of the six edge centers (relative to center)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.edge_position:1 of
msgid "Return the unique position key of an edge."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.edge_position:3 of
msgid ""
"The key is expressed in doubled cube coordinates so that both hexes "
"sharing the edge produce the same integer key."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.edge_tile_references:1 of
msgid "Return `(tile cube, edge direction)` for both hexes sharing an edge."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.edge_tile_references:3 of
msgid "An edge key is `2 * cube + vector`; see `corner_tile_references`."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.hex_center:1 of
msgid "Return the pixel center of the hex at offset position `(column, row)`."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.hex_center:3 of
msgid ""
"The layout leaves half a hex margin at the top and left so that the top "
"tip of the first row and the left edge of the first column are fully "
"visible."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.hex_distance:1 of
msgid "Return the hex distance between two offset positions `(column, row)`."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.hex_distance:3 of
msgid ""
"The distance is the number of hex steps between the positions; it does "
"not depend on the row parity."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.hex_height:1 of
msgid "Return the pixel height of a hex (bounding box height)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.hex_width:1 of
msgid "Return the pixel width of a hex (bounding box width)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.nearest_axis_degrees:1 of
msgid "Return the hex axis degree nearest to `direction` (scratch-style degrees)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.nearest_axis_degrees:3 of
msgid ""
"The six hex axes are 30, 90, 150, 210, 270 and 330 degrees (0 = up, "
"clockwise). Any other angle is snapped to the nearest axis, so one "
"movement step is always exactly one hex. Ties round towards the next "
"higher axis."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.neighbour_offset_deltas:1 of
msgid "Return the offset deltas of the six neighbours for a row parity."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.neighbour_offset_deltas:3 of
msgid ""
"The deltas follow the order of `CUBE_DIRECTIONS`: `\"o\"`, `\"so\"`, "
"`\"sw\"`, `\"w\"`, `\"nw\"`, `\"no\"`. Any integer row can be passed; "
"only its parity counts."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.offset_to_cube:1 of
msgid "Convert odd-r offset coordinates `(column, row)` to cube coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.pixel_to_cube:1 of
msgid "Return the cube coordinates of the hex containing a pixel position."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.ring_offset_deltas:1 of
msgid "Return the offset deltas of all hexes at exactly `radius` distance."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.ring_offset_deltas:3 of
msgid ""
"The order is the ring traversal order of `cube_ring`. For `radius` 0 the "
"only delta is `(0, 0)`; for negative `radius` it is empty. Any integer "
"row can be passed; only its parity counts."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.to_offset:1 of
msgid "Return the offset position of a position tuple, tile, or actor."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_coords.world_pixel_size:1 of
msgid "Return the pixel size of a hex world with `columns` x `rows` hexes."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding:1 of
msgid "Path finding on hexagonal worlds."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding:3 of
msgid ""
"The functions work on the tiles of a `HexWorld`. Stepping onto a tile "
"costs `tile.cost` (default `1`); tiles are impassable if their "
"`is_blocking` flag is set or a blocking actor (`actor.is_blocking`) "
"stands on them. Both rules can be replaced with the `blocked` and `cost` "
"callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding:8 of
msgid ""
"Path finding runs in plain Python on the neighbour cache of the tiles, so"
" it is meant for on-demand queries (a click, a turn), not for being "
"called for hundreds of actors in every frame."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_nearest:1 of
msgid "Return the cheapest path to the nearest hex that satisfies `is_target`."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_nearest:3 of
msgid ""
"A target may be blocked, for example an enemy that blocks its own hex: "
"the path ends on the target. Only the hexes on the way must be passable."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_nearest:9
#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:5
#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.get_reachable_tiles:5 of
msgid "The hex world."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_nearest:10
#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:6
#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.get_reachable_tiles:6 of
msgid "Start hex (position, tile, or actor)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_nearest:14 of
msgid "Optional budget; targets that cost more are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_nearest:15 of
msgid "If `True`, the start hex itself can be the target."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:1 of
msgid "Return the cheapest path between two hexes (A*)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:7 of
msgid "Goal hex (position, tile, or actor)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:8 of
msgid ""
"Optional `blocked(tile) -> bool`; replaces the default rule (tile flag or"
" blocking actor)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:10 of
msgid ""
"Optional `cost(tile) -> float` for entering a tile; replaces `tile.cost`."
" Costs must not be negative."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:12 of
msgid "Optional budget; paths that cost more are not returned."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:13 of
msgid ""
"Cheapest step cost, used to speed up the search. Only needed together "
"with a custom `cost`; a too large value can return a path that is not the"
" cheapest."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.find_path:17 of
msgid ""
"The tiles from start to goal, both included, or an empty list if the goal"
" is blocked, unreachable, or too expensive."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.get_path_cost:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the cost of a path: the sum of the costs of all hexes but the "
"first."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.get_reachable_tiles:1 of
msgid "Return all hexes reachable within a movement budget (Dijkstra)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.get_reachable_tiles:7 of
msgid "Movement budget; with default costs this is the number of steps."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.has_line_of_sight:1 of
msgid "Return whether no blocked hex lies between two hexes."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds.worlds.hex_world.hex_pathfinding.has_line_of_sight:3 of
msgid ""
"Only the hexes strictly between start and goal count, so a blocked goal "
"(for example an enemy that blocks its own hex) can be seen."
msgstr ""

